  "details": "Using flying mode is hard to control when you want to record smooth motion shots. Having pivot points that the camera lens can follow can help with that.\n\nBasically, the function is the same as keyframing an animation in a video editor or Blender. You can choose the speed of the rail, how smooth the movement from each point, and an option to let it loop.\n\nIt would also be useful if zoom value is also recorded in the pivot point.\n\nThis is very useful for content creators and club organizers for scenes involving camera movement.",
